#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:1
msgid "PLUMED Masterclass 21.7: Optimizing PLUMED performances"
msgstr "PLUMED Masterclass 21.7：PLUMED の性能最適化"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:3
msgid "Origin"
msgstr "作成について"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:5
msgid ""
"This masterclass was authored by Giovanni Bussi and Max Bonomi on April 21, "
"2021"
msgstr "この Masterclass は、2021年4月21日に Giovanni Bussi and Max Bonomi によって作成された。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:7
msgid "Aims"
msgstr "目的"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:9
msgid ""
"In this Masterclass, we will discuss how to monitor and optimize the "
"performances of a PLUMED-enhanced MD simulation."
msgstr "この Masterclass では、PLUMED を組み合わせた MD の性能を測定・最適化する方法を扱う。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:11
msgid "Objectives"
msgstr "到達目標"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:13
msgid "Once you have completed this Masterclass you will be able to:"
msgstr "この Masterclass を終えると、次のことができるようになる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:15
msgid ""
"measure the performances of a PLUMED-enhanced simulation using the "
"[DEBUG](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.8/user-doc/html/_d_e_b_u_g.html) "
"action;"
msgstr ""
"[DEBUG](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.8/user-doc/html/_d_e_b_u_g.html) "
"Action で、PLUMED を組み合わせたシミュレーションの性能を測定する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:16
msgid "optimize a metadynamics simulation;"
msgstr "Metadynamics のシミュレーションを最適化する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:17
msgid "optimize GROMACS parallelization;"
msgstr "GROMACS の並列化を最適化する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:18
msgid ""
"define complex CVs in the PLUMED input file in a computationally efficient "
"manner."
msgstr "複雑な CVs を、計算効率のよい PLUMED 入力として定義する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:20
msgid "Setting up PLUMED"
msgstr "PLUMED のセットアップ"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:22
msgid ""
"For this masterclass you will need versions of PLUMED and GROMACS that are "
"compiled using the MPI library. You shoudl thus follow the instructions that"
" are reported for [this earlier "
"masterclass](../../../21/005/data/NAVIGATION.html)."
msgstr ""
"この Masterclass には、MPI ライブラリでコンパイルした PLUMED と GROMACS が必要である。[以前の "
"Masterclass](../../../21/005/data/NAVIGATION.html) の手順に従ってほしい。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:24
msgid ""
"Natively-compiled GROMACS and PLUMED will be significantly faster than the "
"conda versions that we are providing. Since we are focusing on performance "
"here, this might be the right time to learn how to install them on your own."
msgstr ""
"使用する環境でコンパイルした GROMACS と PLUMED は、配布している conda "
"版より大幅に速くなる。この課題は性能に注目するので、自分でのインストール方法を学ぶよい機会である。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:26
msgid "Resources"
msgstr "資料"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:28
msgid ""
"The data needed to execute the exercises of this Masterclass can be found on"
" [GitHub](https://github.com/plumed/masterclass-21-7). You can clone this "
"repository locally on your machine using the following command:"
msgstr ""
"演習に必要なデータは [GitHub](https://github.com/plumed/masterclass-21-7) "
"にある。次のコマンドでリポジトリを自分のマシンに clone できる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:34
msgid ""
"__All the exercises were tested with PLUMED version 2.7.0 and GROMACS "
"2019.6__"
msgstr "__すべての演習は PLUMED 2.7.0 と GROMACS 2019.6 で動作確認されている。__"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:36
msgid "Exercises"
msgstr "演習"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:38
msgid ""
"Notice that the results of these exercises might depend on the details of "
"the hardware and software you are using. It is thus instructive to test them"
" on different architectures, or with different PLUMED or GROMACS versions."
msgstr ""
"結果は使用するハードウェアやソフトウェアの詳細に依存する場合がある。異なる Architectures や、別の PLUMED・GROMACS "
"のバージョンでも試すと学びになる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:40
msgid "Measuring performance"
msgstr "性能の測定"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:42
msgid ""
"In these exercises you will have to maximise the performance of your "
"simulation. When using GROMACS, the common way to report performances is to "
"check at how many ns/day the simulation can produce. At the end of the log "
"file you should find lines like these ones"
msgstr ""
"演習では、シミュレーションの性能を最大化する。GROMACS の一般的な指標は、1日で何 ns 計算できるかを表す ns/day "
"である。ログの末尾には、次のような行があるはずである。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:53
msgid ""
"Here, the higher the ns/day the faster your simulation will be. Another "
"important information it the wallclock time, that indicates how many seconds"
" elapsed since the start of your simulation. If you then run the same input "
"file using PLUMED as well you will instead see something like this:"
msgstr ""
"ns/day が高いほど、シミュレーションは速い。もう1つ重要なのは Wallclock Time、すなわち開始から何秒経過したかである。同じ入力で "
"PLUMED も使うと、次のようになる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:72
msgid "Notice that:"
msgstr "次の点に注目する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:73
msgid "The performance has decreased."
msgstr "性能が低下している。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:74
msgid "The wallclock time has increased."
msgstr "Wallclock Time が増えている。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:75
msgid "PLUMED is reporting some information about the time spent using it."
msgstr "PLUMED の処理にかかった時間の情報が表示されている。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:77
msgid ""
"Notice that the total time spent using PLUMED is approximately equal to the "
"increment in the wallclock time. This might be different when using a GPU "
"(and indeed the increment in the wallclock time should be smaller). This "
"extra time measures the cost of using PLUMED. The goal of this Masterclass "
"is to understand how to decrease this extra time without impacting the "
"result of your simulation."
msgstr ""
"PLUMED の総処理時間は、Wallclock Time の増加分にほぼ等しい。GPU を使うと異なることがあり、Wallclock Time "
"の増加は小さくなるはずである。この追加時間が PLUMED の使用コストを表す。結果に影響せず、この時間を減らす方法を理解することが、この "
"Masterclass の目的である。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:79
msgid ""
"Notice that PLUMED gives a breakdown of the time spent. Some rows correspond"
" to communication, and might become important if you run with a lot of MPI "
"processes. Usually, most of the time is spent in the forward loop, where "
"collective variables are calculated."
msgstr ""
"PLUMED は、処理時間の内訳も示す。通信に対応する行は、多数の MPI Processes "
"で実行すると重要になる場合がある。通常は、Collective Variables を計算する Forward Loop が大半を占める。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:81
msgid ""
"You can obtain a more detailed breakdown adding to your input this line:"
msgstr "入力に次の行を追加すると、さらに詳しい内訳を得られる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:87
msgid "The tail of the log will then look like this:"
msgstr "ログの末尾は、次のようになる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:113
msgid ""
"Notice that for both the forward and the backward loop you are shown with a "
"breakdown of the time required for each of the actions included in the input"
" file. You should recognize the name of the actions that you defined, "
"whereas unnamed actions are referred to with a generic `@`-number that "
"corresponds to their position in the input file. From this detailed log you "
"can also appreciate how often each action has been performed. PLUMED tries "
"to optimize this, e.g., only computing variables when they are needed. This "
"breakdown is very useful to know where you should direct your effort."
msgstr ""
"Forward Loop と Backward Loop の両方について、入力内の各 Action "
"の処理時間が示される。自分で定義した名前を確認でき、無名の Actions は、入力での位置に対応する `@` と番号で参照される。各 Action "
"の実行回数も分かる。PLUMED "
"は、変数を必要なときにだけ計算するなど、これを最適化している。この詳細な内訳は、どこに最適化の労力をかけるべきかを知るために役立つ。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:115
msgid "Exercise 1: Dissociation of NaCl in water"
msgstr "演習1：水中の NaCl の Dissociation"

# Closed the unpaired math delimiter in the source prose without changing the
# expression.
#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:117
msgid ""
"As a first test system we will consider a single Na Cl pair in a water box. "
"The two ions are expected to attract each other, so that the bound "
"conformation should be stable. The free energy as a function of the distance"
" between the two ions should thus have a minimum followed by a barrier. At "
"larger distances, it is not expected to become flat but rather to decrease "
"as $-2k_BT \\log d, due to the entropic contribution, and then to grow again"
" when reaching the boundaries of the simulation box. In this exercise we "
"will compute the free-energy as a function of the distance between the two "
"ions. As collective variables we will use the distance between the two ions "
"as well as the number of water oxygens that are coordinated with the sodium "
"ion."
msgstr ""
"最初のテスト系は、水の Box 内の1組の Na と Cl である。2つの Ions は引き合うため、Bound Conformation "
"が安定なはずである。Ion 間距離の関数としての自由エネルギーには、Minimum と、その先の Barrier "
"が現れると考えられる。大きな距離では平坦にはならず、Entropy の寄与により $-2k_BT \\log d$ のように減少し、Simulation"
" Box の境界付近で再び増加する。この演習では、2つの Ions の距離の関数として自由エネルギーを計算する。CVs には、Ion "
"間距離と、Sodium Ion に Coordinate している水の酸素原子数を使う。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:119
msgid ""
"In the `data/exercise1` folder of the `GitHub` repository of this "
"Masterclass, you will find a `topol.tpr` file, which is needed to perform a "
"MD simulation of this system with GROMACS. You can then create a "
"`plumed.dat` file like this one as a starting point:"
msgstr ""
"この Masterclass の `GitHub` リポジトリの `data/exercise1` に、GROMACS でこの系を計算するための "
"`topol.tpr` がある。まず、次のような `plumed.dat` を作成する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:132
msgid "As usual, you can run a simulation with the following command"
msgstr "通常どおり、次のコマンドでシミュレーションを実行できる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:138
msgid ""
"For the first three points, you can run relatively short simulations, so "
"choose nsteps based on what you can quickly test on your machine. For the "
"fourth point instead you will need to reach convergence. A time on the order"
" of a ns should be more the sufficient."
msgstr ""
"最初の3項目は比較的短い計算でよいので、自分のマシンですぐに試せる nsteps を選ぶ。4項目目は収束が必要だが、1 ns "
"程度あれば十分なはずである。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:140
msgid "Exercise 1a: Optimizing the calculation of a metadynamics bias"
msgstr "演習1a：Metadynamics Bias の計算の最適化"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:142
msgid ""
"For this first point, we will focus on the calculation and update of the "
"metadynamics bias. We will try to have a simulation that runs faster without"
" changing significantly the result. Check the manual of "
"[METAD](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.8/user-doc/html/_m_e_t_a_d.html) and "
"find out how to speed up this calculation. A few hints:"
msgstr ""
"最初は Metadynamics Bias "
"の計算と更新に注目する。結果を大きく変えずに高速化する。[METAD](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.8/user-"
"doc/html/_m_e_t_a_d.html) のマニュアルを調べ、その方法を考えてほしい。ヒントを示す。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:145
msgid ""
"What matters is the deposition rate (that is: height/pace). Increasing the "
"pace and height by the same factor should not change the result "
"significantly."
msgstr ""
"重要なのは追加速度、すなわち height/pace である。pace と height を同じ倍率で増やしても、結果は大きく変わらないはずである。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:146
msgid ""
"Grids will make calculation faster (especially for long runs) but update "
"slower."
msgstr "Grids を使うと、特に長い計算で評価が速くなるが、更新は遅くなる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:148 INSTRUCTIONS.md:157 INSTRUCTIONS.md:166
msgid ""
"Notice that these changes are not expected to impact the convergence of the "
"algorithm. Thus, you do not need a converged simulation to measure the "
"impact on performances."
msgstr "これらの変更は収束性には影響しないと考えられるため、性能への影響を測るのに、収束済みの計算は不要である。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:150
msgid "Exercise 1b: Optimizing the calculation of a coordination number"
msgstr "演習1b：Coordination Number の計算の最適化"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:152
msgid ""
"For this second point, we will focus on the calculation of one of the two "
"biased collective variables, namely the coordination of the Na ion with "
"water oxygens. We will try to have a simulation that runs faster without "
"changing significantly the result. Check the manual of "
"[COORDINATION](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.8/user-"
"doc/html/_c_o_o_r_d_i_n_a_t_i_o_n.html) and find out how to speed up this "
"calculation. A few hints:"
msgstr ""
"2つ目は、Bias を加える CVs の一方、Na Ion と水の酸素との Coordination "
"の計算に注目する。結果を大きく変えずに高速化する。[COORDINATION](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.8/user-"
"doc/html/_c_o_o_r_d_i_n_a_t_i_o_n.html) のマニュアルから方法を調べてほしい。ヒントを示す。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:154
msgid "Neighbor lists might help, but be very careful with parameters."
msgstr "Neighbor Lists が役立つ可能性があるが、パラメータには十分注意する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:155
msgid ""
"Starting with PLUMED v2.7 the construction of neighbor lists is "
"parallelized. Performances might thus be very different if you test your "
"input with PLUMED v2.6 or earlier."
msgstr ""
"PLUMED 2.7 以降、Neighbor Lists の構築は並列化されている。2.6以前で同じ入力を試すと、性能が大きく異なる可能性がある。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:159
msgid "Exercise 1c: Optimizing GROMACS parallelization"
msgstr "演習1c：GROMACS の並列化の最適化"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:161
msgid ""
"For this third point, we will try to make sure that GROMACS runs at its "
"maximum speed. For this you will have to check GROMACS manual. A few hints:"
msgstr "3つ目は、GROMACS 自体が最速で動くようにする。そのためには GROMACS のマニュアルを調べる必要がある。ヒントを示す。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:163
msgid ""
"Based on the number of processors in your computer, play with the number of "
"OpenMP threads and of MPI processes."
msgstr "使用する Processor 数に応じて、OpenMP Threads と MPI Processes の数を変えてみる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:164
msgid "Check if the `-pin on` option improves performances."
msgstr "`-pin on` で性能が改善するかを確認する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:168
msgid "Exercise 1d: Optimizing metadynamics parameters"
msgstr "演習1d：Metadynamics のパラメータの最適化"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:170
msgid ""
"We will now make modifications to the algorithm so as to be able to arrive "
"to the same result running a shorter simulation. Try to play with "
"[METAD](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.8/user-doc/html/_m_e_t_a_d.html) "
"parameters and see if you can improve them. A few hints:"
msgstr ""
"次に、より短いシミュレーションで同じ結果を得られるよう、アルゴリズムを変更する。[METAD](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.8/user-"
"doc/html/_m_e_t_a_d.html) のパラメータを変え、改善を試してほしい。ヒントを示す。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:172
msgid ""
"Changing hills width might affect that speed at which you fill free-energy "
"basins."
msgstr "Hills の幅は、自由エネルギー Basins が埋まる速度に影響しうる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:173
msgid ""
"Limiting the domain of the collective variables that you explore might help,"
" if you can predict what happens in the portion of the domain that the "
"simulation does not explore."
msgstr "探索しない領域で何が起きるかを予測できるなら、CVs の探索範囲を制限すると役立つ場合がある。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:175
msgid "You can even try to reduce the number of CVs."
msgstr "CVs の数を減らすことも試せる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:177
msgid ""
"Notice that these changes are expected to impact the convergence of the "
"algorithm. Thus, you do not need a converged simulation to measure the "
"impact on performances, and you have to make sure that the statistical "
"accuracy is comparable."
msgstr ""
"これらの変更は収束性に影響すると考えられる。そのため、性能への影響を測るのに収束済みの計算は不要だが、統計精度が同程度であることを確認しなければならない。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:179
msgid "Exercise 1e: Computing the binding free energy"
msgstr "演習1e：結合自由エネルギーの計算"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:181
msgid ""
"As a final step, analyze the simulations performed so far to compute the "
"standard binding free energy between the two species. Notice that even "
"though this is defined at 1M concentration, the calculations that you are "
"running are actually at infinite dilution."
msgstr ""
"最後に、ここまでの計算を解析し、2つの化学種の標準結合自由エネルギーを求める。定義上の標準濃度は1 M だが、実行している計算は Infinite "
"Dilution の条件であることに注意する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:183
msgid ""
"Exercise 2: Folding of the C-terminal domain (CTD) of the RfaH virulence "
"factor"
msgstr "演習2：RfaH Virulence Factor の C-terminal Domain（CTD）の Folding"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:185
msgid ""
"In this exercise, we will work with the C-terminal domain (CTD) of the RfaH "
"virulence factor from _Escherichia coli_ that was introduced in the fourth "
"exercise of [this lesson](../../../21/004/data/NAVIGATION.html). This part "
"of the system, which we refer to as RfaH-CTD, undergoes a dramatic "
"conformational transformation from β-barrel to α-helical, which is "
"stabilized by the N-terminal domain of the RfaH virulence factor. This "
"transition is illustrated in the following figure:"
msgstr ""
"この演習では、[以前のレッスン](../../../21/004/data/NAVIGATION.html)の演習4で紹介した、_Escherichia"
" coli_ の RfaH Virulence Factor の C-terminal Domain（CTD）を扱う。RfaH-CTD "
"と呼ぶこの部分は、β-Barrel から、N-terminal Domain により安定化される α-Helical "
"な構造へと、大きく変化する。次の図にこの遷移を示す。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:187
msgid ""
"![Structural transformation of the RfaH-CTD. Domain dissociation is "
"triggered upon binding of the NTD (gray) to its target ops (operon polarity "
"suppressor) element DNA, relieving the autoinhibited state and allowing the "
"transformation of the CTD (colored) from an α-helical hairpin (A) towards a "
"five-stranded β-barrel (B). Note that the NTD and CTD are connected by a "
"linker that does not order within the crystals and therefore is not shown in"
" the figure.](figures/RfaH-CTD.png)"
msgstr ""
"![RfaH-CTD の構造変化。NTD（灰色）が標的の ops（Operon Polarity Suppressor）DNA Element "
"に結合すると、Domain の Dissociation が起きる。Autoinhibited State が解除され、CTD（色付き）は "
"α-Helical Hairpin（A）から5本鎖の β-Barrel（B）へ変化できる。NTD と CTD をつなぐ Linker "
"は結晶中で秩序化しないため、図には示していない。](figures/RfaH-CTD.png)"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:189
msgid ""
"RfaH-CTD is simulated using a simplified, structure-based potential, called "
"[SMOG](https://smog-server.org). The SMOG energy function has been designed "
"to have two local minima corresponding to the β-barrel and α-helical states "
"of RfaH-CTD. To achieve this goal, the SMOG energy function promotes native "
"contacts, i.e. interactions that are present in the native structure(s). "
"When using structure-based force fields, a function of the coordinates that "
"is correlated with the energy of the system, such as the total number of "
"native contacts, has been shown to be a good CV for enhanced-sampling "
"simulations. Unfortunately, these types of CVs often involve a large number "
"of atoms and are therefore computationally expensive to calculate at every "
"step of the simulation. In this exercise, we will learn how to write and "
"optimize these types of CVs."
msgstr ""
"RfaH-CTD は、[SMOG](https://smog-server.org) という単純化した Structure-based "
"Potential で計算する。その Energy Function は、β-Barrel と α-Helical の2状態に対応する Local "
"Minima を持つよう設計されている。Native Structures にある Interactions、すなわち Native Contacts "
"を安定化することで実現している。Structure-based Force Fields では、Native Contacts の総数のような、系の "
"Energy と相関する座標関数が Enhanced Sampling に適した CV "
"となることが示されている。しかし、多くの原子が関わることが多いため、各ステップでの評価は高コストになる。この演習では、そのような CVs "
"の記述と最適化を学ぶ。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:191
msgid ""
"In the `data/exercise2` folder of the "
"[GitHub](https://github.com/plumed/masterclass-21-7) repository of this "
"Masterclass, you will find:"
msgstr ""
"この Masterclass の [GitHub](https://github.com/plumed/masterclass-21-7) リポジトリの"
" `data/exercise2` に、次のファイルがある。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:193
msgid ""
"two PDB files of RfaH-CTD in the β-barrel (`stateA.pdb`) and α-helical "
"(`stateB.pdb`) states;"
msgstr ""
"β-Barrel（`stateA.pdb`）と α-Helical（`stateB.pdb`）の2状態の RfaH-CTD の PDB ファイル。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:194
msgid ""
"a `topol.tpr` file, which is needed to perform a MD simulation of this "
"system with GROMACS;"
msgstr "GROMACS でこの系の MD を実行するための `topol.tpr`。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:195
msgid ""
"a template PLUMED input file (`plumed.dat`) to perform a metadynamics "
"simulation using the total number of native contacts as CV. These contacts "
"are defined using only the β-barrel conformation, which is the most "
"populated state in the conditions we are simulating."
msgstr ""
"Native Contacts の総数を CV として Metadynamics を行う入力テンプレート（`plumed.dat`）。Contacts "
"は、今回の条件で Population が最も大きい β-Barrel Conformation のみから定義している。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:198
msgid "The provided PLUMED input file looks as follows:"
msgstr "付属の PLUMED 入力は、次のようになっている。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:241
msgid "The objectives of this exercise are to:"
msgstr "演習の目的は次のとおりである。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:243
msgid ""
"optimize the distance-based CV provided in the template PLUMED input file. "
"**The user should report the speedup obtained with the optimized CV with "
"respect to the one defined in the provided input file**;"
msgstr ""
"入力テンプレートの距離に基づく CV を最適化する。**元の入力で定義した CV に対し、最適化後の CV がどれだけ高速化したかを報告すること。**"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:244
msgid "optimize the performances of well-tempered metadynamics."
msgstr "Well-tempered Metadynamics の性能を最適化する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:245
msgid ""
"evaluate the stability of the β-barrel state of RfaH-CTD (with error "
"estimate). Have a look at [this earlier "
"lessonr](../../../21/004/data/NAVIGATION.html) for more info."
msgstr ""
"RfaH-CTD の β-Barrel "
"状態の安定性を、誤差推定とともに評価する。詳細は[以前のレッスン](../../../21/004/data/NAVIGATION.html)を参照してほしい。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:247
msgid "Suggestions:"
msgstr "提案："

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:248
msgid ""
"the users should consult the PLUMED manual in order to optimize the proposed"
" CV;"
msgstr "CV の最適化のため、PLUMED のマニュアルを参照する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:249
msgid ""
"the COORDINATION CV can be defined using a custom switching function, whose "
"calculation can be made faster by using [AsmJit](https://asmjit.com). For "
"more information, have a look [here](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.7/user-"
"doc/html/_lepton.html);"
msgstr ""
"COORDINATION CV には、独自の Switching Function を使える。その評価は "
"[AsmJit](https://asmjit.com) "
"で高速化できる。詳細は[こちら](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.7/user-"
"doc/html/_lepton.html)を参照してほしい。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:250
msgid ""
"try [Multiple time stepping](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.7/user-"
"doc/html/_m_t_s.html) to apply the metadynamics bias every 2 or 4 steps "
"using the `STRIDE` option on the "
"[METAD](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.8/user-doc/html/_m_e_t_a_d.html) line."
msgstr ""
"[METAD](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.8/user-doc/html/_m_e_t_a_d.html) 行の "
"`STRIDE` で2または4ステップごとに Bias を加える、[Multiple Time "
"Stepping](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.7/user-doc/html/_m_t_s.html) を試す。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:252
msgid "Please keep in mind that:"
msgstr "次の点に注意してほしい。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:253
msgid ""
"SMOG is significantly less computational demanding than all-atoms, explicit "
"solvent force fields. However, the simulation of this system might take a "
"few hours, so allocate enough time to complete this exercise;"
msgstr ""
"SMOG は All-atom の Explicit-solvent Force Fields "
"より大幅に低コストだが、この系でも数時間かかる場合がある。演習を終えられるよう、十分な時間を確保する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:254
msgid ""
"due to the special nature of the force field, please execute GROMACS using "
"the following command: `gmx mdrun -plumed plumed.dat -ntomp 4 -noddcheck`. "
"You can adjust the number of CPU cores you want to use (here 4, OpenMP "
"parallelization), based on the available resources. The system is not "
"particularly big, therefore using a large number of cores might be "
"inefficient."
msgstr ""
"Force Field の特殊性により、GROMACS は `gmx mdrun -plumed plumed.dat -ntomp 4 "
"-noddcheck` で実行する。資源に応じて CPU Core 数を調整できる。ここでは OpenMP で4 Core "
"を使う。系はそれほど大きくないため、多数の Cores はかえって非効率になる場合がある。"
